# Audit source-backed distant-object transforms

Audit distant-object transforms from source evidence instead of accepting
manual editor placement as world-layout authority.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Audit distant-object transforms from source evidence instead of accepting
  manual editor placement as world-layout authority.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

World placement is derived from authored scenegraph transforms before mesh
publication. Distant-object handling only splits disconnected geometry into
independent visual objects; it does not translate, rotate, scale, or rewrite UV
coordinates. A new regression captures all source positions and UVs before the
split and requires the exact bit-pattern sets after separation.

Existing tests also prove distant components become separate objects, nearby
components stay together, and nested source transforms place drawables at their
authored global position. Narrative map-family grouping adds no spatial offset.
The generated world transform manifest keeps Unreal import translation and
rotation at zero and scale at one, so manual editor placement is not a second
world-layout authority.

Definition-only review meshes may receive deterministic gallery placement below
`review/`, but that namespace is excluded from the normal world import set and
therefore cannot alter production distant-object transforms.
